title:: MIR2
summary:: Native spectral, pitch, onset, tonal, rhythm, auditory and wavelet analysis
categories:: Libraries>MIR

MIR2 provides 132 public classes for real-time musical analysis and analysis-driven sound. Each class page explains the technique, units, timing, limits and an audible example. Most return control-rate features; audio-input analyzers consume the full audio block internally. FFT readers preserve the shared buffer representation.

Pitch confidence, periodicity and voicing describe different evidence. Neither confidence nor tonal/rhythm labels imply calibrated recognition accuracy. Use matching FFT sizes and hops, allow analysis warmup, and increase server real-time memory for large filter banks or CQT kernels.

section:: Core

definitionlist::
## link::Classes/SpecCentroid2:: || Explicit spectral centroid in Hz.
## link::Classes/SpecFlatness2:: || Stable spectral flatness with explicit conventions.
## link::Classes/SpecPcile2:: || Generalized spectral percentile frequency.
## link::Classes/MFCC2:: || Configurable Mel-frequency cepstral coefficients.
## link::Classes/FFTFlux2:: || Explicit frame-to-frame spectral distance.
## link::Classes/Onsets2:: || Classical and SuperFlux onset detection with causal peak picking.
## link::Classes/PitchYIN:: || YIN fundamental frequency with explicit confidence and voicing.
## link::Classes/PitchMPM:: || McLeod Pitch Method with NSDF clarity.
## link::Classes/Periodicity:: || Repeating-structure evidence without a final F0 decision.
## link::Classes/Voicing:: || Binary and continuous voiced/harmonic evidence.
## link::Classes/Pitch2:: || General modern F0 facade with explicit octave ambiguity.
::

