section:: Examples and verification

Class examples use a looping bundled sound, synchronized buffer setup and feature-controlled synthesis, filtering or panning. They can be changed to SoundIn using the commented source line. Each example includes cleanup. Onsets2 now includes the seven classical methods and corrected SuperFlux processing. Representative-recording onset evaluation is deferred to a later stage; numerical checks do not replace listening.

section:: Further work

The initial chord vocabulary is major/minor/no-chord. Neural models, ChromaCQT, extra wavelet families and multiband rhythm transforms remain explicit research gates. See the installed docs/roadmap-status.md for implementation and verification status.
